{#-
  src/ioc-export-by-type.njk — the remote-worker index as CSV, one file per
  indicator type

  Paginates over iocIndex.remote_workers.type_keys, one page per type, each
  writing the pre-built string in iocIndex.remote_workers.csv_by_type (see
  toCsvByType() in src/_data/iocIndex.js). Same columns as
  /assets/data/ioc-index.csv (src/ioc-export.njk), just pre-filtered to one
  ioc_type, so a reader who wants only the email addresses or only the IP
  addresses across the whole dataset — not just what the client-side search
  has currently matched — gets a static, linkable file with no JavaScript
  required. Linked from /remote-workers/.

  No `layout`, so 11ty writes the body verbatim; the whitespace-control
  markers matter the same way they do in src/ioc-export.njk.
-#}
